ok - ledger records render a golden day note, side notes, and replay is a no-op
ok - queue.md renders every bucket from the snapshot and keeps the last good view when it fails
ok - the log reads the fleet snapshot, never data/backlog.md
ok - records split at midnight and a new day carries the previous Open at close
ok - answers nest under their hold on its own day; an unanchored answer lands on its day as re:
ok - inbox notes with a log day thread under each other and carry firstmate's reply
ok - without config/log-tickets nothing is linked as a ticket
ok - manual add is idempotent, learn files a note and a ledger record, unresolved finds nothing missing
ok - the log refuses when off, unreachable, or owned by another home, and replays afterwards
ok - enable turns on the ledger, lays out the log, and warns about a location outside the home
ok - start logs by default, honors off and a folder, and a secondmate home logs to its own data/log
ok - --wait bounds a non-quiet sync's wait for a held lock
